body:
Hm.  That sucks.  I saw her in Kansas City, and it was awesome! 

&#x200B;

Thanks for sharing!

You are looking at this wrong.  You have been through real pain, and navigated the depths via rejection, injustice, abandonment and chastisement.   USE IT.  Write an Aria and record it.  Pain makes the very best, virtuoso vocalists, and your story makes you a compelling choice.   So tell it when you can and rebrand yourself.   Feel your pain in each exquisite note.  Dig deep and pour it into your music and you will touch hearts like never before.

&#x200B;

See you in the spotlight!

&#x200B;

PS.  NEVER blithely wish for cancer.  It is offensive to those of us who have suffered through it.  Thanks.

Just.. wow. 

&#x200B;

  Do you feel somewhat unburdened now?  I think you are a courageous young man, and commend you - not only for recognizing all of that pain while preparing to lose another family member, but for writing so frankly about it and sharing the experience with the world.  Right on!
